{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3185","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3185","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3185\",\"parent_revision\":\"8bd5595f1e45a3d908f950a11d95bba753ba72c8\",\"root_revision\":\"c7afc7955803143b7edd0f05912619636bb062303170afcc81f97ecbb5dc4dfa\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe live E2E suite (`plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py`) is displaced onto an in-memory backend on every test. `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` defines `_isolated_backend` as `autouse=True`, function-scoped, calling `set_config(BacklogConfig(backend=ProviderMemoryBackend()))`. It carries no `e2e` exemption, while its sibling autouse fixture in `plugins/development-harness/conftest.py` has an explicit `if request.node.get_closest_marker(\\\"e2e\\\"): return`.\\n\\n`live_items` installs the real `GitHubBackend` at class scope. `_isolated_backend` is function-scoped, so it runs after and overwrites it. `set_config` is a last-writer-wins module singleton, and teardown calls `reset_config()`, which clears rather than restores.\\n\\nVerified with `pytest --setup-plan -n0`:\\n\\n```\\nSETUP    C live_items\\n  SETUP    F _isolated_backend\\n```\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nOnly issue creation still reaches GitHub, through a backend-independent path. Every other operation the suite claims to exercise end-to-end \u2014 list, view, update, groom, sync, pull, close, resolve \u2014 runs against a stub.\\n\\nTwo tests pass vacuously as a result. `test_l8_sync_push_groomed` and `test_l9_pull_refresh_from_github` assert only `isinstance` checks, and route into `ProviderMemoryBackend.reconcile`, which records the request and returns an empty result. Neither can fail for a product reason. They are the two reported as passing in a run where the lifecycle is broken.\\n\\nThe backend is function-scoped, so each test also starts with an empty one \u2014 an item created in one test is absent in the next.\\n\\nThe consequence for planning: repairing the current failures without fixing this produces a green E2E job that validates nothing. Green for the wrong reason is worse than red, because red prompts someone to look.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: E2E design review, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA separate defect compounds it: the real GitHub error from a failed create is recorded into `result[\\\"warnings\\\"]` and never printed, so no CI log has ever contained the reason the current failure happens. Six distinct failure signatures are on record for this job; no single-cause explanation covers them.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Not Established\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nWhy `_try_create_github_issue` returns `None` today. It returns `None` on two different branches in `operations.py` and no log distinguishes them. This is the first thing that has to be learned, and nothing downstream should be built before it is.\\n\\nWhether the network guard still ignores `DH_ALLOW_TEST_NETWORK=1` as it did in one recorded signature. `git log -L` on the guard range shows the code unchanged since it was introduced, so it was not fixed by a later change \u2014 but the current failure path never reaches a blocked call, so still-firing and no-longer-firing are equally consistent.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nWhy `_try_create_github_issue` returns `None` today. It returns `None` on two different branches in `operations.py` and no log distinguishes them. This is the first thing that has to be learned, and nothing downstream should be built before it is.\\n\\nWhether the network guard still ignores `DH_ALLOW_TEST_NETWORK=1` as it did in one recorded signature. `git log -L` on the guard range shows the code unchanged since it was introduced, so it was not fixed by a later change \u2014 but the current failure path never reaches a blocked call, so still-firing and no-longer-firing are equally consistent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## User Provided Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nA full design with three costed approaches, a recommendation, sequencing, and a validation plan built on external-client controls is written to `.tmp/scratch/reports/20260823-e2e-design.md`. Its TDD verdict is REQUIRED, with three named tests that must fail before the corresponding change lands. Treat that document as input to grooming, not as an approved plan.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nA full design with three costed approaches, a recommendation, sequencing, and a validation plan built on external-client controls is written to `.tmp/scratch/reports/20260823-e2e-design.md`. Its TDD verdict is REQUIRED, with three named tests that must fail before the corresponding change lands. Treat that document as input to grooming, not as an approved plan.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ba1e7db617d35f49d67b1d8cb6e98179caa5449e13a1214019d649cfbf94c89c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQTR_1Q\"}"}